// Validate and clean email for display purposes
static cleanEmailForDisplay(email: string): string {
  return email.replace(/\+[a-zA-Z0-9]{25}/, "");
}

async getOutputRecurringSeatedBookings(bookingsIds: number[], showAttendees: boolean) {
  const databaseBookings = await this.bookingsRepository.getByIdsWithAttendeesWithBookingSeatAndUserAndEvent(bookingsIds);

  const bookingsMap = new Map(databaseBookings.map(booking => [booking.id, booking]));

  const transformed = bookingsIds.map(bookingId => {
    const databaseBooking = bookingsMap.get(bookingId);
    if (!databaseBooking) {
      throw new Error(`Booking with id=${bookingId} was not found in the database`);
    }
    return this.getOutputRecurringSeatedBooking(databaseBooking, showAttendees);
  });

  return transformed;
}

getHost(user: DatabaseUser | null) {
  if (!user) {
    return {
      id: "unknown",
      name: "unknown",
      email: "unknown",
      displayEmail: this.getDisplayEmail("unknown"),
      username: "unknown",
    };
  }

findings.body:
`getOutputRecurringSeatedBookings` used to return `transformed.sort((a, b) => new Date(a.start).getTime() - new Date(b.start).getTime())`. The PR replaces this with `return transformed;`, which is not related to the displayEmail change. The method feeds `bookings.service.ts` around line 611, the GET-by-uid path for recurring seated bookings. The order of `bookingsIds` comes from the repository query, which does not sort by time. So a client can now receive the instances of a recurring seated booking in an arbitrary order. The sort also still exists in `getOutputRecurringBookings` and `getOutputRecurringSeatedBookings`' sibling methods, so this looks accidental.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="411-425"}

Restore the sort or document why the order no longer matters. Add an e2e assertion on order for recurring seated bookings so this does not regress again.

`getDisplayEmail` uses `email.replace(/\+[a-zA-Z0-9]{25}/, "")`. The pattern has no `$` anchor and no lookahead, so it removes the first `+` followed by any 25 alphanumeric characters. It does not require the match to be the whole suffix before `@`. An ordinary user address with a plus-tag of 25 or more alphanumerics, for example `a+abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz1234@x.com`, becomes `a1234@x.com`, which is wrong. The regex also matches in the domain part of an address if one contains `+`. There are no unit tests for `getDisplayEmail` edge cases. The PR relies on the regex matching `google-calendar.service.ts`, but that does not make it correct for every address.

::code{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="96-98"}

Tighten the pattern to match only the local-part suffix before `@`, for example `/\+[a-z0-9]{25}(?=@)/i`, and add unit tests for: no suffix, a suffix on a multi-segment local part, a legitimate short plus-tag, and a 25+ character user tag.

`bookingTransformed.bookingFieldsResponses.guests.map(this.getDisplayEmail)` passes the method without binding `this`. It works today only because `getDisplayEmail` does not read `this`. A later change that uses an instance member inside the helper would fail silently at runtime. The sibling block in `getOutputRecurringBooking` uses an arrow function, so the two blocks are inconsistent.

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="158-174"}

Use an arrow function, as the recurring variant does: `.map((guest: string) => this.getDisplayEmail(guest))`.

`BookingAttendee.cleanEmailForDisplay` is added to the DTO class with the same regex as `getDisplayEmail`. Nothing calls it. The comment "Validate and clean" is also misleading, because the method neither validates nor is called from a validator. The result is two copies of the same regex that can drift apart.

::code{file="packages/platform/types/bookings/2024-08-13/outputs/booking.output.ts" lines="59-62"}

Delete the static method. If the regex needs to be shared, move it to one exported constant and import it into both the service and the DTO.

Several `required` arrays in `docs/api-reference/v2/openapi.json` were edited so that the `"required": [` key starts at column 0, not at the indentation of the surrounding keys. The JSON is still valid, but the file no longer matches the generated style, and the diff is noisy. It appears at least at lines 31729, 31833, 32267, and 33370. The PR also says the OpenAPI spec was auto-generated, so these hand edits suggest the generated output and the checked-in file are out of sync. Regenerate the file from the DTOs rather than editing it by hand.

::code{file="docs/api-reference/v2/openapi.json" lines="31726-31734"}

Regenerate the OpenAPI document with the project's generator, or re-indent these blocks to match their neighbours.

The same `displayEmail` and `displayGuests` block is copied into `getOutputBooking` and `getOutputRecurringBooking`. The two copies already differ in style, with one using `this.getDisplayEmail` directly and the other using an arrow function. The seated and create paths compute `displayEmail` inline in other places. Any future field, for example a new guest-shaped array, will need the same copy-paste in every method.

::code{file="apps/api/v2/src/ee/bookings/2024-08-13/services/output.service.ts" lines="158-174"}

Move the logic into one private method, for example `addDisplayFields(bookingTransformed)`, and call it from each output method.
